      "question_order": 1,
      "question_text": "Which activation function is most commonly used in hidden layers of Deep Neural Networks to prevent vanishing gradients?",
      "explanation": "ReLU outputs zero for negative inputs and identity for positive inputs, preventing derivative saturation.",
      "points": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "80000000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002",
      "quiz_id": "70000000-0000-4000-a000-000000000501",
      "question_order": 2,
      "question_text": "What is the primary role of the Backpropagation algorithm?",
      "explanation": "Backpropagation applies the chain rule backward from loss to compute gradients for parameter updates.",
      "points": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "80000000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003",
      "quiz_id": "70000000-0000-4000-a000-000000000501",
      "question_order": 3,
      "question_text": "In Convolutional Neural Networks, what does a Max Pooling layer do?",
      "explanation": "Max pooling takes the maximum value in a window grid, downsampling features while preserving translation invariance.",
      "points": 10
    }
  ],
